    {
      "id": "notable",
      "title": "Notable Entries",
      "content": "<h3>Volester</h3><p>Weak to <strong>Ice</strong>, no resistances. One of the simplest enemies to counter - just bring Ice and it folds.</p><h3>The Chevaliere family works differently per variant</h3><ul><li><strong><a href=\"/steel-chevaliere\" style=\"color:var(--accent);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:2px\">Steel Chevaliere</a></strong> - weak to <strong>Physical</strong>, resists nothing</li><li><strong><a href=\"/gold-chevaliere\" style=\"color:var(--accent);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:2px\">Gold Chevaliere</a></strong> - weak to <strong>Light and Dark</strong>, resists Fire and Ice</li><li><strong><a href=\"/ceramic-chevaliere\" style=\"color:var(--accent);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:2px\">Ceramic Chevaliere</a></strong> - weak to <strong>six elements at once</strong> (Fire, Ice, Lightning, Earth, Dark, Light), which makes it the most permissive target in the game</li></ul><h3>Watch the Earth absorbers</h3><p><strong><a href=\"/gault\" style=\"color:var(--accent);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:2px\">Gault</a>, <a href=\"/glaise\" style=\"color:var(--accent);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:2px\">Glaise</a> and <a href=\"/pelerin\" style=\"color:var(--accent);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:2px\">Pelerin</a></strong> all absorb an element while being weak to Fire or Ice. Attacking with the wrong type is worse than doing nothing.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "how-to-use",
      "title": "How to Use This Table",
      "content": "<ul><li><strong>Check before swapping weapons.</strong> Weapon damage type determines far more than raw attack power against these enemies</li><li><strong>Never attack an absorber.</strong> The Absorbs column is the one that loses fights</li><li>Bosses are listed separately - see the <a href=\"/boss-guide\">boss guide</a> and the <a href=\"/boss-order\">boss order</a> pages for boss-specific resistances</li></ul>"
    }
